Okay.

01:00.000 --> 01:02.000
Okay.

01:30.000 --> 01:30.760
Okay.

01:30.940 --> 01:34.720
So let's talk about the one lie that everybody gets told every single day.

01:35.600 --> 01:37.600
That hustle is the only path to success.

01:38.860 --> 01:40.640
Now, to start off, I want to give you a quote.

01:40.860 --> 01:44.220
It's a book that I've read probably three or four times and I need to read again.

01:44.300 --> 01:45.260
It's called The Topic Habits.

01:45.880 --> 01:46.660
James Clear says,

01:47.220 --> 01:49.260
You don't rise...

01:49.260 --> 01:50.000
God damn it.

01:50.680 --> 01:51.900
Those fucking trucks.

02:00.000 --> 02:12.160
Let's talk about one of the biggest lies people get sold every single day.

02:12.640 --> 02:14.700
That hustle is the only path to success.

02:14.700 --> 02:31.440
Let's talk about one of the biggest lies people get sold every single day.

02:32.000 --> 02:34.180
That hustle is the only path to success.

02:34.740 --> 02:38.580
I read a book a couple of years ago and I still need to read it a couple more times.

02:38.960 --> 02:40.900
It's called The Topic Habits by James Clear.

02:42.420 --> 02:44.360
You don't rise to the level of your goals.

02:44.700 --> 02:46.500
You fall to the level of your systems.

02:47.280 --> 02:50.740
Now, let's kind of try to break that down and see what he means by that.

02:50.900 --> 02:54.640
Overall, when you have a goal, that is an end point.

02:54.980 --> 03:01.240
When you have systems, that actually provides direction to get to that end point.

03:02.040 --> 03:10.200
Now, it may seem like it's a simple idea, but it is monumentous when you actually put the effort to understanding it.

03:10.200 --> 03:21.480
Even just identifying bottlenecks in your workflow or in your business or your 9 to 5 grind, whatever it is that you are doing right now.

03:21.480 --> 03:29.840
Identifying the bottlenecks in your business is just basically the first step in figuring out the very first part of your system.

03:29.980 --> 03:31.440
You're going to have many systems.

03:31.620 --> 03:32.940
You're going to have algorithmic systems.

03:33.080 --> 03:37.200
You're going to have a checklist system, listicles, all kinds of things.

03:37.200 --> 03:40.900
A system doesn't mean AI or automation.

03:41.140 --> 03:49.060
A system is an overall approach to how you think and how you actually tackle whatever problems you're experiencing, whether it's life, business, or otherwise.

03:49.060 --> 03:55.020
With the last module, we went over mapping out workflows.

03:55.020 --> 04:01.040
That gives you kind of the framework to building AI automations and that particular system.

04:01.360 --> 04:04.300
But overall, how does your business run end to end?

04:04.700 --> 04:07.480
Who do you have on your client intake?

04:07.580 --> 04:08.980
Who's on your marketing team?

04:09.060 --> 04:09.840
Do they have a system?

04:10.320 --> 04:13.740
Your sales team and RevOps, what is their system?

04:14.380 --> 04:17.260
Do they all cohesively work together or not?

04:17.260 --> 04:22.860
If not, that's how you first identify bottlenecks and that's how you also create the workflows.

04:23.000 --> 04:26.340
But overall, when you start to think in systems, it actually changes the game.

04:28.780 --> 04:42.920
The number one reason why hustle isn't the only thing that's needed is because you actually need systems to do the hustle.

04:42.920 --> 04:46.420
Hustle just becomes checking emails every day.

04:46.620 --> 04:51.120
Or did I follow with that lead last week that had the potential to make me $10,000 or $15,000?

04:51.660 --> 04:52.740
Or did you forget?

04:52.840 --> 04:54.300
Did you not even send out the proposal?

04:54.640 --> 05:03.200
If you have a system in place and you actually can go step by step and you do it the same way every single time, then hustle doesn't feel like a game of just straight up whack-a-mole.

05:03.200 --> 05:13.720
You actually have these things in place that keep you on task, on point, and make sure that you actually do either come close to or hit and crush your goals.

05:13.880 --> 05:19.020
Without the systems, your goals are pointless and hustle alone isn't going to get you there.

05:19.020 --> 05:26.860
Once you start to do this, clarity comes in.

05:27.020 --> 05:29.260
You start to understand the bigger picture.

05:29.620 --> 05:37.400
If you are a founder or an owner, when you have a system to check whether or not other people have their systems in place,

05:37.600 --> 05:42.620
then everything comes from the top down and you get organized in your organization.

05:42.620 --> 05:50.940
With that clarity, you know what matters.

05:51.040 --> 05:52.060
You know what doesn't matter.

05:52.340 --> 05:57.480
And if you're familiar with the 80-20 principle, 20% of your profits or your revenue comes from 80% of your work.

05:58.360 --> 05:59.240
Did I say that backwards?

06:00.440 --> 06:00.860
Yeah.

06:01.680 --> 06:05.620
And if you understand the Pareto principle, the 80-20, 20-20...

06:05.620 --> 06:09.180
Jesus, I can't even speak now.

